## Summary

Implemented a persistent, file-based tutor chat history store per (course, module).

**New files:**
- `src/lib/schemas/chatHistory.ts` — Zod `ChatHistory` (`schemaVersion: 1` + `messages[{role: user|assistant, content, createdAt}]`), plus a permissive `ChatHistoryWrite` schema (allows `role: 'error'`) and `CHAT_HISTORY_MAX_MESSAGES = 200`.
- `src/lib/server/chatHistory.ts` — path resolution (`~/.ai-lecturer/chats/<courseSlug>/<moduleId>.json`, overridable via `CHATS_ROOT_OVERRIDE`, slug-guarded), `readChatHistory` (returns empty on missing **or** invalid file, logs a warning, never throws → no 500), `normalizeChatHistory` (strips `error` messages, trims to last 200), `writeChatHistory` (atomic write via existing `atomic.ts`, lazy dirs, last-write-wins).
- `src/app/api/chats/[courseSlug]/[moduleId]/route.ts` — GET (history, 400 on unsafe slug) and PUT (422 invalid payload, 400 bad JSON/slug, full overwrite).
- `src/lib/server/chatHistory.test.ts` — 12 tests covering roundtrip, corrupt file, invalid content, limit trimming, error-message exclusion, and invalid-PUT rejection.

**Key design decision:** the persisted schema only permits `user|assistant`, while the PUT payload schema additionally accepts `error` so the UI can submit its full transcript without a 422 — the server strips error messages before writing. This satisfies both "error messages not persisted" and "reject invalid PUT".

**Quality checks:** 12/12 tests pass, `tsc --noEmit` clean, eslint clean. No `ui` tag, so browser testing was skipped per instructions. prd.json `US-210.passes` set to `true` and committed (`18658ab`).
